风吹新竹 Wind Through Hsinchu — Scrapbook Song (手账歌谣), a NEO-Cine library demo

SONG: 《风吹新竹》, words, music and vocals by hoy neo (2026).
  audio/song-excerpt.mp3 is the part of the song the film uses (146.0–196.0 s of the 205.92 s song, 160 kbps); the film
  plays 146.64–195.20 s of it, faded in over 0.25 s and out over 2.6 s, levelled to -14 LUFS; nothing else is changed.
  data/lyrics.json holds the song's 48 lyric lines with the timings checked for the original music video (simplified).
  data/audiomap.json holds the beat grid, downbeats and drum hits the original video was timed against (the whole song,
  and the 30 s clip of the final chorus, analysed with librosa through HyperFrames' music-to-video); a new film is
  analysed with the kit's own tools/analyze.py instead.

PICTURE AND CODE: from the hand-drawn music video for 风吹新竹, part of this library under its licence.
  - ../kit/: the Scrapbook Song kit (drawing, lyric carriers, scene layer, page player, tools).
  - scripts/scenes/ (the bridge and final-chorus scenes, the end card) and scripts/assets/ (the characters, the Hsinchu
    props, the night street, songlib.py): this song's own drawings. A film in this style draws its own.
  - The page player ../kit/page/gsap-lite.js evaluates the scenes' GSAP-style timelines as a pure function of time;
    GSAP itself is not used or shipped.
  Drawn entirely in code (SVG generated in Python, rendered in a browser). No photographs, scans, AI-generated images,
  video or 3D models. The East Gate (东门城) and the other Hsinchu props are drawn from their general shape; this is not
  an official depiction of any place.

